> A hand-checkable calculation

For positive advantage2 and ratio1.5, epsilon.2 clips the surrogate to2.4 instead of3. The source compares this clipped objective with a KL-penalty alternative.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ppo_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
