> Interpret time-limit bootstraps carefully

The source rollout collector marks only actual terminals as done, but retains auto-reset observations for time-limit successors. Using the true saved final observation would give a more exact bootstrap. This inherited approximation is retained and visible; the GAE API itself requires the caller to supply the correct final-state value. Collection and episode splitting remain report code.

> Actual episode returns

Each series is one original comparison/worker-policy training run, in the source execution order. These are captured task returns, not fabricated convergence curves or intrinsic-bonus totals. One logged point does not establish a trend.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ppo_return.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/ppo_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int series=0;for(const auto& [key,tensor]:archive){if(!key.starts_with("return_"))continue;auto values=tensor.to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x;for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)x.push_back(i+1);plot.lines(x,values,key,{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50}).points(x,values,key+" points",{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50},4);++series;}plot.title("ppo actual return diagnostics").x_label("Ended training episode").y_label("Task return").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/ppo_return.svg");}
